---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Notice from "../components/ui/Notice.astro";
import { SITE, CONTACT, LEGAL_UPDATED } from "../consts";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles data.`}
  lede={`Last updated ${LEGAL_UPDATED}.`}
>
  <Notice title="Read this first">
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an independent, experimental project run by one individual. It is
      not a company or a commercial service, and it is provided as is, with no
      warranty of availability, retention, or confidentiality.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Do not upload confidential, regulated, or personal data.</strong>{" "}
      Account deletion is not self-serve yet; until it is, email us and your data will
      be removed.
    </p>
  </Notice>

  <p>
    This notice explains what the Project collects, why, and what is not done with
    it. It covers this website and the {SITE.name} application.
  </p>

  <h2>Who operates the Project</h2>
  <p>
    The Project is run by a single individual in a personal, non-commercial capacity,
    not by a company. Where data-protection law would treat someone as the
    "controller" of data processed here, that is the maintainer personally. For any
    privacy question or request, email us using the address at the bottom of this
    page.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details.</strong> When you create an account: your name, email
      address, and authentication identifiers from the sign-in provider. Used to
      identify you and protect your workspace.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Content you upload.</strong> Documents, datasets, prompts, and the
      models trained from them. Stored so the Project can process them for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operational data.</strong> Job records, resource usage, and error logs.
      Used to debug and to keep the environment running.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Aggregate site analytics.</strong> Non-identifying traffic counts for
      this website. No advertising or cross-site tracking.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not submit anyone else's personal data. If you do, you are acting as
    that data's controller and are responsible for having a lawful basis to process
    it here.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it is processed</h2>
  <p>
    Data is processed only to operate the Project for you — to authenticate you, run
    the jobs you request, show you results, and keep the system working and secure.
    Where a lawful basis is required, it is the performance of the agreement you
    entered into by using the Project, and the maintainer's legitimate interest in
    keeping it running and secure.
  </p>

  <h2>How your content is used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your data is <strong>not</strong> used to train any model of the maintainer's,
      and is not pooled with other users' data.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your data is <strong>not</strong> sold, rented, published, or shared for
      advertising.
    </li>
    <li>
      Content is scoped to your own workspace so other accounts cannot reach it.
    </li>
    <li>
      The maintainer claims no ownership of your data, models, or their outputs. See
      the <a href="/terms">terms</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Infrastructure providers</h2>
  <p>
    Running the Project requires a small number of third-party providers — hosting,
    object storage, databases, GPU compute, and authentication. They process data
    only as needed to deliver their part of the system, under their own terms and
    security practices.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Those providers operate in various countries, including outside your own, so data
    may be stored or processed abroad — including in the United States. Protections
    available in your jurisdiction may not apply once data is held elsewhere. Using
    the Project means accepting that, which is another reason not to upload sensitive
    data.
  </p>

  <h2>Model provider API keys</h2>
  <p>
    You can use the default model endpoints or configure your own provider API key. A
    key you configure is <strong>encrypted at rest</strong> (AES-256-GCM), is never
    displayed back to you in full, and is used only to sign requests you initiate.
    Those requests reach the provider you selected, under that provider's terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    The honest assurance is that keys are encrypted. If you spot anything in the code or behaviour that could leak a
    credential, please email us to get that fixed rather than disclosing it publicly.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Content is kept while your account is active. You can delete datasets, models,
    and other artifacts in the app; that removes them from active systems, and
    backups age out on their ordinary cycle. Account-level deletion is not yet
    self-serve — email us and your account and associated data will be removed.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is encrypted in transit, access is authenticated, and stored provider
    credentials are encrypted at rest. That said, this is an experimental project run
    by one person: <strong>
      no guarantee against compromise, unauthorised access, or accidental exposure is
      given or implied,
    </strong> and there is no formal incident-response or breach-notification
    programme. Where the law requires notification of a breach, reasonable efforts
    will be made to comply, but no timeframe is promised.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Project is not intended for anyone under 18, and accounts should not be
    created by them. If you believe a minor has provided data here, email us and it
    will be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, export, or
    delete your personal data, to withdraw consent, and to object to certain
    processing. Email us and your request will be handled. You may also have the
    right to complain to your local data-protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website stores only what is needed to remember your theme preference. The
    application uses cookies required for sign-in and session management. No
    advertising or cross-site tracking cookies are used.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This notice may change. The date above always reflects the current version, and
    there is no notification mechanism — check back here rather than expecting to be
    told.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.admin}`}>{CONTACT.admin}</a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
